## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/bokeh.html
- Summary (EN): Simulates a lens's out-of-focus highlights by spreading each pixel's light across an aperture-shaped area. Unlike a blur, which averages surrounding pixels, it distributes each pixel's light outward according to that pixel's own scale.
- Résumé (FR) : Étale la lumière de chaque pixel sur une forme d'ouverture pour imiter les reflets flous d'un objectif, au lieu de moyenner les voisins comme un flou.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: image to apply the effect to", "aperture (optional): mono mask defining the spread shape; a circle is used when unwired", "radiusscale (optional): per-pixel scale for bokeh size, clamped to 1", "mask (optional): per-pixel mask amount scaled by the Mask parameter"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type accepted by the source", "Bokeh Map Filter: filters the aperture map for higher-quality results", "Mask: how much of the new value mixes with the original (default 1, only the new value)", "Toggle RGB, Red, Green, Blue, Alpha: channels the effect applies to", "Radius: maximum bokeh radius in pixels", "Bokeh Gain: boosts or reduces the total luminance of the result", "Bokeh Resolution: resolution the aperture is resampled to, which speeds up filtering of large apertures", "Normalize Gathered Light: divides gathered light by the number of contributing pixels to reduce halos between large and small bokeh"]

- Caveats: ["Large Radius values are computationally expensive because much scattering is required", "The aperture is normalized, so total brightness is preserved by default; Bokeh Gain is needed to change it", "Normalize Gathered Light reduces halos but does not preserve energy", "radiusscale is clamped to 1 and cannot scale bokeh above that"]

